+### FLUJO
+
+[FLUJO](https://github.com/mario-andreschak/FLUJO) can connect to a running Graphiti MCP server over Streamable HTTP.
+
+1. Complete the [server configuration](#configuration) and [start Graphiti](#running-the-server) with a supported database.
+2. In FLUJO, open **Connected Apps** and select **Connect App**.
+3. Select **I have connection details**, then **At a remote URL**.
+4. Enter `http://127.0.0.1:8000/mcp/` when FLUJO and Graphiti run on the same machine. Otherwise, use a Graphiti endpoint reachable from the FLUJO backend.
+5. Select **Connect**. After the connection test passes, select **Update server**.
+6. Open the new server card, select **Tools**, choose `get_status`, and select **Test tool** to check the database connection.
+
+To read existing episodes, choose `get_episodes`, enter the appropriate `group_ids`, and select **Test tool**. These checks validate connectivity and episode retrieval; memory ingestion and semantic search require the model-provider configuration described above.
+
